---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import ModelStatusTracker from '../../components/ModelStatusTracker.jsx';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="AI Model Status Tracker"
  description="Live status check for OpenAI, Anthropic, and Google Cloud AI — see if an outage is on their end before you debug your own code."
>
  <ModelStatusTracker client:load slot="tool" />

  <h2>Is it down for everyone, or just you?</h2>
  <p>
    When an AI API call fails, it's easy to assume it's a bug in your code
    — but sometimes the provider itself is having an incident. This page
    checks each provider's public status feed server-side (bypassing
    browser CORS restrictions) so you get a fast, unified view.
  </p>

  <h2>AI Model Status FAQ</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>How often does this update?</strong> The page auto-refreshes
    every 60 seconds, and you can manually refresh anytime.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Where does this data come from?</strong> Each provider's public
    status page API — the same data source their own status pages use.
  </p>
</ToolLayout>
